---
interface Props {
  compact?: boolean;
}

const { compact = false } = Astro.props;
const layers = [
  {
    "id": "input",
    "label": "Input",
    "short": "What is encoded",
    "text": "Tokenization, retrieved context, and instruction order shape what enters the system. Missing relationships can keep evidence out before reasoning starts.",
    "source": "Recall Debt",
    "url": "/research/recall-debt/"
  },
  {
    "id": "representation",
    "label": "Representation",
    "short": "What the model can express",
    "text": "Internal representations are part of the causal route. A stable signal or a successful intervention does not by itself identify the construct we named.",
    "source": "Control and representation",
    "url": "/questions/control-has-grammar/"
  },
  {
    "id": "harness",
    "label": "Harness",
    "short": "What context survives",
    "text": "Memory, prompts, classifiers, tools, and delegation route capability. Decomposition can remove the very context a monitor needs.",
    "source": "Factor(U,T)",
    "url": "/research/factor-ut/"
  },
  {
    "id": "action",
    "label": "Action",
    "short": "What changes the world",
    "text": "Code, experiments, and control signals give outputs consequences. The action changes what the next observer will encounter.",
    "source": "From proposal to bench",
    "url": "/work/pop2-protein-expression/"
  },
  {
    "id": "evaluation",
    "label": "Evaluation",
    "short": "What counts as evidence",
    "text": "A reward needs a trace and adjudication. The verifier must be able to reject the optimizer’s claimed success, and its own validity remains a question.",
    "source": "Eval Evidence",
    "url": "/work/eval-evidence/"
  },
  {
    "id": "institution",
    "label": "Institution",
    "short": "Who can contest success",
    "text": "Institutions allocate resources and authority. My open question: can independent evaluators preserve correction when incentives favor the same answer?",
    "source": "Distributed corrigibility · hypothesis",
    "url": "/questions/inside-the-loop/#section-7"
  },
  {
    "id": "time",
    "label": "Time",
    "short": "What the next loop inherits",
    "text": "People and systems adapt to one another. Decisions become context, infrastructure, and future data; memory needs lineage if later correction is to remain possible.",
    "source": "Handoffs are memory",
    "url": "/questions/handoffs-are-memory/"
  }
];
---

<section class:list={["loop-lab", compact && "loop-lab-compact"]} aria-labelledby={compact ? "loop-title-compact" : "loop-title"}>
  <div class="shell loop-shell">
    <div class="loop-copy">
      <p class="overline">The same object · seven altitudes</p>
      <h2 id={compact ? "loop-title-compact" : "loop-title"}>One output,<br />{" "}<span>seven layers of cause.</span></h2>
      <p class="loop-intro">Trace an output into action, evidence, and the conditions of its next use. Each layer links to work or a question; the institutional extension remains a hypothesis.</p>
      {!compact && <a class="all-work-link" href="#section-1">Read the full argument <span>↓</span></a>}
    </div>

    <div class="loop-stage" data-loop-stage>
      <svg class="loop-orbit" viewBox="0 0 600 600" aria-hidden="true">
        <defs>
          <marker id="loop-arrow" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto" markerUnits="strokeWidth"><path d="M0,0 L0,6 L7,3 z" /></marker>
        </defs>
        <circle cx="300" cy="300" r="216" />
        <path d="M300 62 A238 238 0 0 1 538 300" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />
        <path d="M538 300 A238 238 0 0 1 300 538" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />
        <path d="M300 538 A238 238 0 0 1 62 300" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />
        <path d="M62 300 A238 238 0 0 1 300 62" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />
      </svg>
      <div class="loop-center">
        <span data-loop-short>{layers[0].short}</span>
        <strong data-loop-label>{layers[0].label}</strong>
        <p data-loop-text>{layers[0].text}</p>
        <a class="loop-source" data-loop-source href={layers[0].url}>{layers[0].source} →</a>
      </div>
      {layers.map((layer, index) => (
        <button
          class:list={["loop-node", index === 0 && "active"]}
          style={`--node-index:${index}; --node-count:${layers.length}`}
          type="button"
          data-loop-node
          data-label={layer.label}
          data-short={layer.short}
          data-text={layer.text}
          data-source={layer.source}
          data-url={layer.url}
          aria-pressed={index === 0 ? "true" : "false"}
        >
          <span>0{index + 1}</span>{layer.label}
        </button>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll("[data-loop-stage]").forEach((stage) => {
      const label = stage.querySelector("[data-loop-label]");
      const short = stage.querySelector("[data-loop-short]");
      const text = stage.querySelector("[data-loop-text]");
      const source = stage.querySelector("[data-loop-source]");
      const nodes = Array.from(stage.querySelectorAll("[data-loop-node]"));
      const activate = (node) => {
        nodes.forEach((item) => {
          item.classList.remove("active");
          item.setAttribute("aria-pressed", "false");
        });
        node.classList.add("active");
        node.setAttribute("aria-pressed", "true");
        if (label) label.textContent = node.getAttribute("data-label") || "";
        if (short) short.textContent = node.getAttribute("data-short") || "";
        if (source) {
          source.textContent = `${node.getAttribute("data-source")} →`;
          source.setAttribute("href", node.getAttribute("data-url") || "/notes/");
        }
        if (text) text.textContent = node.getAttribute("data-text") || "";
      };
      nodes.forEach((node) => node.addEventListener("click", () => activate(node)));
      let touchX = 0;
      let touchY = 0;
      stage.addEventListener("touchstart", (event) => {
        touchX = event.touches[0].clientX;
        touchY = event.touches[0].clientY;
      }, { passive: true });
      stage.addEventListener("touchend", (event) => {
        const deltaX = event.changedTouches[0].clientX - touchX;
        const deltaY = event.changedTouches[0].clientY - touchY;
        if (Math.abs(deltaX) < 40 || Math.abs(deltaX) < Math.abs(deltaY) * 1.2) return;
        const current = nodes.findIndex((node) => node.classList.contains("active"));
        const step = deltaX < 0 ? 1 : -1;
        activate(nodes[(current + step + nodes.length) % nodes.length]);
      }, { passive: true });
    });
  </script>
</section>
